<title>UK: Banco Real to launch dollar bond next week-lead.</title>
<headline>Banco Real to launch dollar bond next week-lead.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Banco Real is expected to launch a $200 million two-tranche Eurobond next week, lead manager WestMerchant Bank said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was expected that one tranche will be for $125 million with a three-year maturity and the second tranche for $75 million with a four-year maturity, the statement said.</p>
<p>Market talk was for the three-year issue to have a spread in the region of 175-195 basis points over U.S. Treasuries and the four-year issue to have a spread of 190-210 basis points.</p>
<p>Banco Real has not issued a bond since October 1995. It is rated B1 by Moody's rating agency.</p>
<p>--Chris Young,  London Newsroom  +44 171 542 7970</p>
